  "question": {
    "text": "For what values of $\\mathrm{x}$, the function $\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=\\mathrm{x}^4-4 \\mathrm{x}^3+4 \\mathrm{x}^2+40$ is monotone decreasing?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$0 < x < 1$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1 < x < 2$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 < x < 3$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$4 < x < 5$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: $f^{\\prime}(x)=4 x^3-12 x^2+8 x=4 x\\left(x^2-3 x+2\\right)$ $=4 x(x-1)(x-2)$\n<img src=\"assets\\st0088_7bc4d9f5da2b.png\"><br>\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{x}$ is decreasing for $\\mathrm{x} \\in(1,2)$"
  }
}